From: kevin03L <kevin03L@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] irqchip/gic: read the CPU number for the primary GIC only

gic_cpu_init() calls smp_processor_id() up front but uses it only to set up the CPU map of the
primary GIC. A secondary GIC, such as Tegra210's AGIC, is set up from a platform driver probe,
in preemptible context, so with CONFIG_DEBUG_PREEMPT every boot logs

  BUG: using smp_processor_id() in preemptible [00000000] code: (udev-worker)/423
  ...
   gic_cpu_init+0x2c/0x100
   gic_init_bases+0xcc/0x1e0
   gic_of_init_child+0x84/0x160
   gic_probe+0x114/0x1fc

Read it where it is used. The primary GIC is initialised with preemption disabled, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-gic.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-gic.c
@@ -488,7 +488,7 @@ static int gic_cpu_init(struct gic_chip_data *gic)
 {
 	void __iomem *dist_base = gic_data_dist_base(gic);
 	void __iomem *base = gic_data_cpu_base(gic);
-	unsigned int cpu_mask, cpu = smp_processor_id();
+	unsigned int cpu_mask, cpu;
 	int i;
 
 	/*
@@ -500,6 +500,7 @@ static int gic_cpu_init(struct gic_chip_data *gic)
 		/*
 		 * Get what the GIC says our CPU mask is.
 		 */
+		cpu = smp_processor_id();
 		if (WARN_ON(cpu >= NR_GIC_CPU_IF))
 			return -EINVAL;
 
